w: For- ty days and for- ty nights Thou wast fast- ing in the wild;
w: Sun- beams scor- ching all the day; Chil- ly dew\-- drops night- ly shed;
w: Should not we Thy sor- row share And from world- ly joys ab- stain,
w: Then if Sa- tan on us press, Je- sus, Sa- vior, hear our call!
w: So shall we have peace di- vine: Ho- lier glad- ness ours shall be;
