w: For- ty days and for- ty nights Temp- ted, and yet un- de- filed.
w: Prow- ling beasts a- bout Thy way; Stones Thy pil- low; earth Thy bed.
w: Fasting with un- ceas- ing pray- er, Strong with Thee to suf- fer pain?
w: Vic- tor in the wil- der- ness, Grant we may not faint nor fall!
w: Round us, too, shall an- gels shine, Such as min- is- tered to Thee.
w: That with Thee we may ap- pear At the eter- nal East- er- tide.
